   "source": "# Finetune \u2014 Gemma 4 E4B agent distillation (QLoRA \u00b7 Unsloth)\n\nFree-tier Kaggle run. **Before running:** open the right sidebar \u2192 *Settings* \u2192\nset **Accelerator = GPU (T4 \u00d72 or P100)** and **Internet = On**.\n\nOptional *Add-ons \u2192 Secrets*: `HF_TOKEN` (if base weights are gated) and `GOOGLE_API_KEY`\n(lets the free teacher LLM enrich the dataset). Without them the run still works from the\ncommitted seed exemplars. Then **Run All**."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 1. Install dependencies"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "# Kaggle images ship torch/transformers; add the fine-tuning stack.\n!pip install -q --no-deps unsloth unsloth_zoo\n!pip install -q trl peft accelerate bitsandbytes jsonschema\n!pip install -q --upgrade transformers   # Gemma 4 support"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 2. Pull the project code\nClones this repo into the session and puts `src/` on the path. Idempotent: it skips the\nclone if `src` is already importable (e.g. attached as a dataset)."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "import os, sys, subprocess\n\nREPO_URL = \"https://github.com/Sachin0496/Finetune.git\"\nREPO_DIR = \"/kaggle/working/Finetune\"\n\ndef have_src():\n    try:\n        import src  # noqa: F401\n        return True\n    except Exception:\n        return False\n\nif not have_src():\n    if not os.path.isdir(os.path.join(REPO_DIR, \"src\")):\n        subprocess.run([\"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth\", \"1\", REPO_URL, REPO_DIR], check=True)\n    sys.path.insert(0, REPO_DIR)\n\nimport src  # noqa: F401\nprint(\"project code ready\")"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 3. Build the dataset\nGenerates and validates the multi-task data (deck-plan JSON \u00b7 animation HTML \u00b7 tool calls)."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "from src import config\nfrom src.data.build_dataset import build, self_check\n\nself_check()\nsummary = build(config.DATA.n_train, config.DATA.n_val, config.DATA.seed)\nsummary"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 4. QLoRA fine-tune\nUnsloth 4-bit + LoRA on Gemma 4 E4B. The adapter is saved under `/kaggle/working/outputs`."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "from src.train.train_qlora import train\nadapter_dir = train()\nadapter_dir"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 5. Before / after evaluation\nBase vs fine-tuned valid-output rates plus a side-by-side sample gallery."
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "from src.eval.evaluate import evaluate\nmetrics = evaluate()\nmetrics"
  },
  {
